<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Afrasiyabids of Mazandaran</h1><p class="st-meta">1349 CE – 1359 CE (approx.) · capital Amol</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The ten-year rule of Kiya Afrasiyab Chelavi, who murdered the last Bavand ruler and took Amol before falling to the Mar'ashi sayyids.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiya-afrasiyab">Kiya Afrasiyab</a> of the Chelavi family was a commander and in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fakhr-al-dawla-hasan">Fakhr al-Dawla Hasan</a>, the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bavand-dynasty">Bavand dynasty</a>. In 1349 he murdered Hasan and took control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amol">Amol</a> and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrasiab">Afrasiyab's</a> brief rule is known mainly from Mazandarani chronicles such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zahir-al-din-marashi">Zahir al-Din Mar'ashi's</a> history. He tried to win support from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> followers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qavam-al-din-marashi">Sayyid Qavam al-Din Mar'ashi</a>, then turned against them when their influence grew.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1359 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiya-afrasiyab">Afrasiyab</a> and his sons were killed fighting the Mar'ashi dervishes, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qavam-al-din-marashi">Qavam al-Din Mar'ashi</a> founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/marashi-dynasty">Mar'ashi dynasty</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amol">Amol</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/afrasiyabids-of-mazandaran.jpg" alt="Afrasiyabids of Mazandaran" width="320" height="209"><figcaption>Image: محک · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chalav_Government.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1349 CE – 1359 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Amol</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kiya Afrasiyab</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mazandarani, Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Afrasiyab dynasty, Chelavid dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1354&amp;focus=afrasiyabids-of-mazandaran" aria-label="Afrasiyabids of Mazandaran on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5996 862 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Afrasiyabids of Mazandaran lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6316 1118L6333 1115M6316 1118L6316 1118"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6333 1115h0M6316 1118h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6316 1118h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6316 1118h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Amol. <a href="/atlas?year=1354&amp;focus=afrasiyabids-of-mazandaran">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
